## Why This Is Asked

Assesses practical mastery of Azure AD risk-based access controls at scale, including how to design policies, test them safely, and rollback without service disruption.

## Key Concepts

- Identity Protection risk scoring
- Conditional Access policies
- MFA and device compliance
- Session controls and continuous access evaluation
- SIEM integration and audit trails
- Safe rollback and access-review processes

## Code Example

```json
{
  "conditionalAccessPolicy": {
    "displayName": "Risk-based admin access",
    "conditions": {
      "users": { "include": ["admin@contoso.com"] },
      "signInRiskLevels": ["high","medium"],
      "platforms": { "include": ["All"] }
    },
    "grantControls": {
      "builtInControls": ["mfa","deviceCompliance"],
      "sessionControls": ["requireUserConsent","limitSessionDuration"]
    },
    "applications": ["https://portal.contoso.com/admin"]
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate these policies in a sandbox before production?
- How would you measure impact on admin productivity and detect policy drift?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical implementation of PIM for cross-tenant vendor access scenarios; validates understanding of governance, auditability, and emergency access controls in real-world incident response environments.

## Key Concepts
- Privileged Identity Management (PIM)
- Eligible vs Active assignments
- Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)
- Approval workflows
- Just-in-time activation
- Conditional Access integration
- Audit logging and monitoring
- Automatic revocation mechanisms
- Cross-tenant access patterns
- Time-bound access controls
- Compliance reporting

## Code Example
```javascript
// PIM activation request configuration
const pimRequest = {
  roleId: 'incident-admin-role',
  justification: 'Critical incident response - vendor access required',
  duration: 'PT4H', // 4 hours maximum
  ticketInfo: {
    system: 'ServiceNow',
    ticketId: 'INC001234',
    ticketUrl: 'https://company.service-now.com/incident'
  },
  approvers: ['security-team@company.com'],
  mfaRequired: true,
  activationType: 'just-in-time'
};

// Monitor PIM activation logs
function monitorPIMActivations() {
  return {
    startTime: '2024-01-15T10:00:00Z',
    endTime: '2024-01-15T14:00:00Z',
    filters: {
      activity: 'Activate',
      targetResources: ['incident-portal-app'],
      initiatedBy: 'external-vendors'
    }
  };
}
```
